            {
                "entry_id": "2f330166-76fd-3b87-af1e-c45753d7ca9c",
                "word": "swole",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                        "entry_id": "2f330166-76fd-3b87-af1e-c45753d7ca9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "simple past and past participle of swell: swelled; swollen."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Southern-US",
                            "also",
                            "form-of",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac911c5c-530e-4259-af98-3ff25552f440",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "His arm just swole up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d21a65b5-cc7b-462f-b60b-b0b5e96aa95a",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "I ate until my belly had swole."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8380c64-6de6-4bd9-9164-f833eca8028f",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "Mildly it [the wind] kiſt our ſailes, and, freſh, and ſweet, / As, to a ſtomack ſterv’d, whoſe inſides meete, / Meate comes, it came; and ſwole our ſailes, when wee / So joyd, as Sara’ her ſwelling joy’d to ſee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03437cb3-d79a-4a6c-a386-c0156b18a729",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "If you drinks a drop more, Miss Lucy, you'll just go like my pore young sister goed, [...] Pop she did not. She swole … swole and swole. [...] I say she swole—and what is more she swole clean into a dropsy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "474591f0-d762-454c-b7da-c033a848b43d",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "[M]y tongue swole up and gagged me and my eyes blurred over with blood […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3644e822-45c0-45e1-bac7-770d9373d089",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "Then they had this guy with clap, a light case of clap, and they gave him inoculations and his balls swole up, they swole up as big as basketballs, they swole and swole so he couldn't walk and they had to take him out of here on a board with these big globes sticking up in the sheet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0c46c71-0815-4e41-b583-b6526ad9e306",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "[A] man from White County had the dropsy? You know, somethin' wrong with his heart and him swole up all over? Uncle Alva said the man at the ho-tel said the man come up there swole up all over like he'd bust if you stuck a pin in him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55b706a1-c26e-4094-a3de-c2488ad9ca72",
                                "sense_id": "ef2f5c42-75bb-34c5-abcd-4b5d2b023865",
                                "text": "She had overheard her Mom and Mrs. Thomas from across the street talking about someone who was allergic to stings, and Mrs. Thomas had said, \"Ten seconds after it gut im, poor ole Frank was swole up like a balloon. If he hadn't had his little kit with the hyperdermic^([sic]), I guess he woulda choked to death.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
